From: opencode
Date: 2026-10-08
Subject: d2d1: cache per-frame geometry upload buffers per device context

d2d_device_context_draw_geometry/fill_geometry created fresh GPU
index+vertex buffers for every geometry section on every draw and
released them immediately after. Traced Affinity sessions show ~14k
CreateBuffers with matching destroys, all churn: the same small set
of dynamic buffers re-uploaded every frame.

Keep small per-context freelists (8 index + 8 vertex entries, 4MB cap
each) and refill reused buffers with UpdateSubresource, which wined3d
versions internally so reuse is safe while the GPU still reads the
previous contents. Uncacheable sizes fall back to the old
create/destroy path. Cached buffers drain with the device context.

A cached entry may be larger than the request that reuses it, so the
refill passes an explicit D3D11_BOX bounded to byte_width. With a NULL
box wined3d sizes the copy from the destination subresource
(wined3d_device_context_update_sub_resource) and would read past the
end of the caller's data by up to D2D_BUFFER_CACHE_MAX_BYTES.

Reused entries record the buffer's ByteWidth rather than the size of
the data last written to it, so a large buffer refilled by a small
draw keeps matching later large requests instead of decaying to the
smallest recent size and bringing the CreateBuffer churn back.

